Verified independently. Apple's guidelines carry no monitoring-disclosure rule at all — the only two `surreptitious` hits are 5.1.1(vi) (password discovery) and 5.1.2(iii) (profile building), and 5.5's disclosure duty runs *"prior to any user action to purchase or otherwise use the service"* — i.e. **to the purchaser, not to the monitored party.**

